---
source: crates/splot/src/types/mod.rs
expression: "format!(\"{}\\nWanViaTargets: [Home, Home.lan] → {duplicate}\",\nmessages.join(\"\\n\"))"
---
Ipv4Network: "10.0.0.1" → missing '/' in: '10.0.0.1'
Ipv4Network: "10.0.0.0/33" → invalid prefix 10.0.0.0/33: must be 0-32
Ipv4Network: "10.0.0.300/24" → invalid address '10.0.0.300/24': invalid IPv4 address syntax
Ipv4Network: "10.0.0.1/24" → 10.0.0.1/24 is not a network address
Ipv4Interface: "10.0.0.0/24" → 10.0.0.0/24 is a network address, expected host address
Ipv4Interface: "10.0.0.255/24" → 10.0.0.255/24 is a broadcast address, expected host address
Ipv4Interface: "x/24" → invalid address 'x/24': invalid IPv4 address syntax
Port: "x" → invalid port format: invalid digit found in string
Port: "0" → port number cannot be 0
PortRange: "x-80" → invalid port: invalid port format: invalid digit found in string
PortRange: "80-22" → range is invalid, it should be {lower}-{higher}
PortRange: "80" → missing '-' in port range
PortOrRange: "x" → invalid port: invalid port format: invalid digit found in string
PortOrRange: "80-22" → invalid port range: range is invalid, it should be {lower}-{higher}
ServicePort: "x" → invalid port: invalid port format: invalid digit found in string
ServicePort: "80-22" → invalid port range: range is invalid, it should be {lower}-{higher}
ServicePort: "1000-1010:2000-2005" → both ranges should have same width: 1000-1010 and 2000-2005
ServicePort: "80:1000-1010" → invalid translation: should never be port:range (80:1000-1010)
Identifier: "" → identifier is empty
Identifier: "a b" → invalid character ' ' at position 1
Identifier: "spl_x" → identifier starts with reserved prefix "spl_"
NestedIdentifier: "abc" → missing '.' separator — qualified names have the form 'Node.Local'
NestedIdentifier: "a.b.c" → too many '.' separators — qualified names have exactly two segments
NestedIdentifier: ".b" → invalid node segment: identifier is empty
NestedIdentifier: "a.b c" → invalid local segment: invalid character ' ' at position 1
AllowFromRef: "a b" → invalid allowFrom reference: invalid character ' ' at position 1
AllowFromRef: "a.b.c" → invalid qualified allowFrom reference: too many '.' separators — qualified names have exactly two segments
WanViaTarget: "a b" → invalid wan target: invalid character ' ' at position 1
WanViaTarget: "a.b.c" → invalid qualified wan target: too many '.' separators — qualified names have exactly two segments
MacAddress: "gg:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff" → invalid hex digit 'g'
MacAddress: "aa:bb" → expected 17 characters, got 5
MacAddress: "aa|bb|cc|dd|ee|ff" → unexpected delimiter '|', should be either ':' or '-'
MacAddress: "aa:bb-cc:dd:ee:ff" → mixed delimiters: started with ':' found '-'
Hostname: "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa.aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa.aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa.aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa" → 254 characters long, at most 253 allowed
Hostname: "a..b" → empty label (a dot at either end, or two in a row)
Hostname: "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa.net" → label "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa" is longer than 63 characters
Hostname: "a_b.net" → invalid character '_' in "a_b" (only letters, digits and hyphens)
Hostname: "-a.net" → label "-a" starts or ends with a hyphen
Hostname: "10.0.0.300" → the last label is all digits
EndpointHost: "a_b.net" → neither an IPv4 address nor a host name: invalid character '_' in "a_b" (only letters, digits and hyphens)
Setting<FirewallProgram>: "iptables" → "iptables" isn't a firewall program splot knows: fw4, nftables, or none
Os: "windows" → "windows" isn't an OS splot knows: openwrt, linux
SshDestination: "" → empty
SshDestination: "-oProxyCommand=sh" → starts with '-', which ssh would read as an option
SshDestination: "root@router -p 2222" → contains ' ': no spaces or control characters
WanViaTargets: [Home, Home.lan] → node 'Home' appears more than once — each node should appear at most once in wan.via
